& [VerbatimUserMessage] is the preserved dictation
  + [text] is "this needs to be tied in to the inference window in such a way that Cantor has a memory function for carrying the persistent attention objects of accountability, available to query in inference... and I'm wondering how that would be referenced... I don't think a hash is right, this is forward-facing, demanding to be attended to in full, a list."

& [ProvisionalArticulation]
  + [name] is Accountability Register
  + [placement] is a trusted forward-facing register regenerated into every governed inference frame
  + [reference] is a stable readable typed handle and not a content hash
  + [completeness] is the complete member roster for the declared basket scope
  + [record_shape] is handle type differentiators current state active roles obligations uncertainty and version
  + [query] is exact-handle expansion from the durable Identity Ledger
  + [hash_role] is integrity and version evidence behind the record rather than its inference-facing identity
  + [boundary] is KV cache and model context are projections while the external ledger remains authority
